WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.968
-Dan, have you ever seen

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.836
anything like this
in your career?

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.538
-No, Jimmy, I have not.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.673
You know, I've been blessed
to live this long.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:11.611
I'm 89 years old,
and I've seen a few things

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.579
over the years,
including the Great Depression,

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:17.917
World War II, Watergate, 9/11 --
so many things.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.386
I've never seen
anything like this.

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:23.189
You know, my reaction, I think,

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.658
was the most common reaction
of the day.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.160
I cannot believe
that I'm seeing this.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.129
I can't believe
I'm watching this.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.264
As I believe you mentioned
somewhere along the way,

00:00:32.264 --> 00:00:35.001
it was like watching
a very bad horror movie --

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.836
horror movie for our country.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:40.073
-And, no, I've never seen
anything like this before.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.542
And neither has any other
American, thank God.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.977
And let us hope
we never see it again.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:47.846
-The last I heard is that
the Senate wanted to go back in

00:00:47.846 --> 00:00:50.683
as soon as they can
and continue and get the count.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.953
What happens now with the vote?
-Well, what happens now,

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:57.757
I would say, Jimmy, having
talked as we have seriously

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.892
about what happened today
with the mob violence

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:02.395
and the mob storming
into the Capitol,

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.197
history is going to record --

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:08.467
Today's big headlines are,
sometime late tonight

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:13.172
or sometime tomorrow,
the Biden election

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:15.541
is going to be certified
by the Congress.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.510
The Congress is gonna
have their vote,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.879
certifying
the Electoral College vote,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:24.149
and Joe Biden will be
officially, formally,

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:27.619
the new president-elect
of the United States,

00:01:27.619 --> 00:01:30.590
and Kamala Harris will be
the new vice president-elect.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.459
That's going to be --
You know, that's set.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.695
And history will record that
as the big headline.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:40.065
The second headline is that
the Democrats are gonna control

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:43.870
the Senate, if these results
in Georgia hold,

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.338
and this is the way it looks.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:48.207
There are gonna be two new
Democratic Senators in Georgia.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.343
And, you know, this --

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.245
this is a whole new day
for the country.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.781
In 13 days,
we have a new president,

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:58.317
new vice president, and if
the Georgia results hold,

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:01.487
which I expect they will,
this Senate will be controlled

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:02.988
by the Democrats,

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:05.625
since Kamala Harris
has the swing vote.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.960
It's going to be a new day
for the country.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:12.265
And those who took part in
storming the Capitol today,

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:16.769
history will footnote them, but
it will footnote them in shame.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.506
The real people, the real heroes
of this democracy today

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:25.811
are, one, my old friend,
the late John Lewis,

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:29.481
Ms. Abrams,
Stacey Abrams in Georgia,

00:02:29.481 --> 00:02:32.418
and all those people who,
in the runoff election,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.454
in both parties,
did what they're supposed to do.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:41.160
They knocked on doors to take
part in a Democratic process.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.230
And once the count, the final
count's in, they accept it.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.332
These are the heroes
of this day.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.367
These people
who've shamed themselves

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.237
and shamed our country
by storming our Capitol

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:56.242
and going inside and taking part
in violence inside the Capitol

00:02:56.242 --> 00:03:00.313
are the ones that should be
shamed today, and that's --

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:02.648
that really should be
the news of the day.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:06.385
Unfortunately, we're gonna be
distracted for some time

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:08.954
by this nastiness
that happened at the Capitol.

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:13.359
-Do you think Trump
really believes that he --

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:17.330
the election was rigged, or does
he have a different agenda?

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.099
-I do not.
I will say,

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:23.335
"How could I know what's in
Donald Trump's heart?"

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:26.105
I don't.
And the straight answer

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:29.675
to your question, I think he
knows exactly what he's doing.

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.511
I think he knows he lost.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:34.113
He's the quintessential
poor loser.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:37.316
I think he, all along,
took the attitude,

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:42.054
"If I don't win the vote,
then I'm gonna try to make sure

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:44.890
that nobody accepts
the honest vote."

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.893
I think he's known
what he's doing all along.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.827
I think he knows
what he's doing now,

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:51.698
and I think he's feeling
very good about himself,

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:54.901
because today,
he got the whole headlines,

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:58.938
the whole attention,
all came to him and his movement

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.908
away from the fact that Biden
had won the election

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.610
and that two new
Democratic Senators

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.912
had been elected in Georgia,
apparently,

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.814
and the Democrats
will control the Senate.

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.549
So I think he's feeling
pretty good about himself

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:12.551
at this moment.

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:16.289
-What's next
for President-elect Biden?

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.591
He has to unite the country.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.792
How does he do that?

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.960
How do we move forward
as a country?

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.263
What's at stake here?

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.599
-Well, what's at stake
is the very future

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.100
of the United States of America.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.071
You know, we have had
the world's most successful

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.974
democratic government, the most
successful democratic government

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.542
in the history of the world,

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.578
that ours is
a constitutional republic

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:42.548
based on the principles
of freedom and democracy.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.383
The question has always been,

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:46.218
"Can we hold ourselves
together?"

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:49.989
And that is the major challenge
of the Biden administration,

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:54.160
and it's no small challenge,
because well over 75 million,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.663
76 million Americans
voted for Donald Trump.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:02.568
And trying to re-establish
some normal amount of unity

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.904
in a country,
in a situation we're in now,

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:07.673
is a tremendous challenge
for President Biden.

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:10.275
I do think he has to make
the decision pretty early

00:05:10.275 --> 00:05:14.080
whether he is to be
a transitional president

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.649
or a transformational president.

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:19.185
That is, is he just gonna be
sort of a president

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.921
who re-established some norms

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.590
but just was waiting
for the next president

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.060
to be really transformative,
or is he gonna try to be

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.662
a transformational president?

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.564
A lot of that depends
on what happens

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.833
with those
within the Republican Party.

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.968
How many of those
in the Republican Party

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:42.174
hold on to the Trump fantasy and
try to keep Trumpism in control,

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:44.910
or do they take their party
in a different direction?

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.948
But the challenge for Biden
right away is to decide

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.917
and to act upon
whether he's transitional

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:56.656
or whether he's just a
transformational president.

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:59.859
-Dan, I thank you for
all the years of your work

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:03.095
in journalism, and I also want
to thank you for your tweets,

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:06.899
because they are calming

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:10.903
in a lot of this craziness
that's surrounding us.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:15.141
And I thank you again for being
on our program tonight.

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:16.542
-I really appreciate that,
Jimmy.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.343
I would like to leave it
on an up note,

00:06:18.343 --> 00:06:19.778
and I think we should.

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:23.616
You know, we all sang or used to
sing "God Bless America."

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:26.418
"God bless America,
stand beside her and guide her

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:30.289
through the night with the light
from above and from within."

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:32.925
We might not sing it tonight,
but we might want to hum it

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.893
and just play the words over
in our head,

00:06:34.893 --> 00:06:38.064
because if we hold steady,
we're gonna be okay.

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:40.499
-My thanks to Dan Rather.
You can see season eight

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:41.934
of his show,
"The Big Interview,"

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:44.904
Wednesdays at 8:00 p.m.,
on Access TV.

